# REQUIRES: verilator
# Staged and multicycle evaluation (`stage-levels`, `multicycle`) of a class
# whose paged register state is kept off chip (--storage <model>:pages=hbm).
# The copy reads its fetch buffer at an evaluation's read position, the
# stages before its state pass, so each instance's pages are fetched by that
# position (the fetch a lead before it, as early as the copy's read position
# before: the buffer is free once that one has read it; but after the frame
# before's write-back of each page), and waited for there (the frame's
# advance checks the instance's pending pages at the read position); the
# write-back is loaded at the state pass with the last stage's values, its
# pages written after it as before. With a window, each prefetch is at the
# copy's read position a window before, and the fetch from the window a lead
# before the read. With page engines, the reads are placed by the read
# positions. Against the target (tb_pages.sv: a controller model per virtual
# memory, answers 1 to 60 host cycles on, `free` low at times, stalls,
# bubbles, PROTOCOL for a read or write of an instance whose read is
# outstanding), from zero state (Driver/Inputs/paged_staged: registered
# outputs, a RAM read through a register): staged; multicycle; bubbles with
# overlapped frames; copies under nested sequencers, and multicycle; the
# dense page word
# (its old value crosses the stages); a window, also multicycle with nested
# sequencers and a short lead; page engines; the leaves' RAM virtual too.
# Waiting for the pages at the state pass instead mismatches MC (seed 1,
# PROTOCOL at seed 3); fetching a lead before the state pass instead of the
# read mismatches ST and MC at every seed; fetching a page before the frame
# before's write-back of it (no s - ii + 2 bound: it binds in CP and CPMC, two
# instances a copy) reads the old page (PROTOCOL and MISMATCH in CP).
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/paged_staged
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/st --static --page 2 --storage Leaf:pages=hbm --stage-levels 1 Leaf > %t/st.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ST < %t/st/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -I%t/st -Mdir %t/st/obj %S/Inputs/tb_pages.sv top.sv %t/st/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/st/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/st/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/st/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+2 +lo=1 +hi=40 +stall=20 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/st/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=20 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/mc --static --page 3 --storage Leaf:pages=hbm --multicycle Leaf:3 --stage-levels 1 Leaf > %t/mc.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MC < %t/mc/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -I%t/mc -Mdir %t/mc/obj %S/Inputs/tb_pages.sv top.sv %t/mc/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/mc/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/mc/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/mc/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+2 +lo=1 +hi=40 +stall=20 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/mc/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=20 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/bub --static --page 3 --storage Leaf:pages=hbm --bubbles --modulo --page-hbm-column-bits 32 --stage-levels 1 Leaf > %t/bub.log 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -I%t/bub -DBUBBLES -DVM1 -Mdir %t/bub/obj %S/Inputs/tb_pages.sv top.sv %t/bub/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/bub/build.log 2>&1
